\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Positioning of Orbis against related categories of academic-support systems. \emph {Push} means the system surfaces an obligation before a student asks. \emph {Unstructured rules} means handling free-text regulation, not only schema-based requirements.\relax }}{3}{}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Official baseline and comparator validity. \emph {Direct} means the same task and data family; \emph {partial} means a related subsystem metric but different domain or output schema; \emph {contextual} means useful for positioning only.\relax }}{4}{}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Dataset and post-processing statistics. The Proactive Event System operates only on the 935 regulatory chunks; all other categories are routed to the RAG search index.\relax }}{5}{}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Event Extraction Pipeline Funnel\relax }}{12}{}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Assignments generated per real student profile, broken down by urgency and matching path. ``SQL'' counts deterministic conditional matches; ``CTX'' counts contextual LLM matches.\relax }}{13}{}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Metric provenance and limitations. Artifact paths are reported relative to the repository.\relax }}{15}{}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Confusion matrix of the event extraction pipeline against gold ground truth ($N{=}323$).\relax }}{15}{}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Binary classification metrics for the event extraction stage. Positive class = true obligation accepted by the system.\relax }}{15}{}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces Per-profile assignment matching scores against gold ground truth ($N{=}712$ pairs: 4 profiles $\times $ 178 accepted obligations).\relax }}{16}{}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Submission agent results stratified by case type. Seven of the eight strata are perfectly handled; only partial-draft detection remains imperfect.\relax }}{17}{}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces Submission agent confusion matrix on $N{=}32$ cases (positive class: approve). Zero false negatives: no genuine submission was rejected. Both false positives are \texttt {flag\_partial} drafts.\relax }}{17}{}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {12}{\ignorespaces Submission agent binary classification metrics (positive class: approve), measured on the 32-case ground-truth set against the current two-call agentic reviewer.\relax }}{17}{}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {13}{\ignorespaces Submission Agent Ablation Study: Redesigning the reviewer significantly lifted in-document prompt-injection resistance because the agent now explicitly verifies whether requirements are met, bypassing embedded adversarial instructions.\relax }}{18}{}%
